{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/963795-heroes-and-conspiracies","id":963795,"title":"Heroes and Conspiracies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-05T10:57:24-07:00","id":963795,"title":"Heroes and Conspiracies","content":"The book describes Heroes as seeing Hunters as basically canon fodder, while Hunters think that Heroes are twisted versions of what they could become (or akin to slashers so to speak).<br /> <br /> I'm curious to know what the forum thinks of what the major conspiracies might think of Heroes from their own perspectives and directives. For Example--<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Task Force Valkyrie has a standing order to observe<br /> but not engage with any independent Heroes they encounter.<br /> Heroes pose too great a risk to equipment and personnel just<br /> by jumping into a fight they have no way of winning (that the<br /> hunters see). -Page 204- </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ashwood Abbey in particular seeks Heroes out to<br /> find quarries for their legendary hunting parties, treating them<br /> like the proverbial hound after the fox. -Page 204- </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Members of the Union frequently end up in Hero-inspired mobs. Conversely, mortals<br /> find their way to the Union or other compacts and conspiracies<br /> as a hunter after a Hero leads their normal, everyday life into<br /> the deep, dark places they never knew existed before. -Page 204- </div> </div> </div>Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10141-solaris","name":"Solaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T17:05:14-07:00","id":963979,"title":"","content":"Well, my personal take is that, if a hunter and a hero ever met? The hunter would simply assume that the hero was merely another hunter instead of something different. After all, the overwhelming majority of Hero abilities really aren't anything extrodinary - the flashiest of which maybe a &quot;relic&quot; weapon for killing monsters, or knowing the trick to opening the gateway into the shadow-realm where monsters hide, neither of which are exactly unheard of by hunters. Certainly, heroes are less obviously magical than a human psychic, let alone an Endowment. <br /> <br /> So, I imagine that the major conspiracies would look at Heroes as simply rival conspiracies in the same line of work with little difference. Maybe a bit obsessed with one type of supernatural, but that's pretty common with a number of Conspiracies, like the Cannite Heresy or the one that punches demons with magical tats. <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Task Force Valkyrie: </i>&quot;Bunch of crazy vigilantee thrill seekers. We take up the Vigil to protect American citizens from the nasties that go bump in the night. These guys are in it just for the glory. Like the government would let them get recognition for murdering something that's not supposed to exist. Still, they seem to have a sixth sense for tracking down hives of extra-human criminal activity, making them excellent informants.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Aegis Kai Doru</i>: &quot;They often claim to have magical talismans and relics that were recovered from the homes of these slain monsters, but all efforts to retrieve these relics for study have ended in failure. Further study is recommended.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Ascending Ones:</i> &quot;Diplomacy is a key strategy of ours, while these so-called heroes are more interested in fighting. Good for watching your back when shit hits the fan, but not so good to keep the street wars to a minimum.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Lucifuge</i>: &quot;Most of their targets seem to be living productive lives in the same way we do, using dark powers to protect people. I even met one that called me sister. He was cut down simply for being born different. Watch your back, unless these heroes decide we're part of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Malleus Malificorum</i>: &quot;God helps those who help themselves. These warriors choose to fight against the darkness, driven by dark fears they have trouble bringing up even in confession. Lend a helping hand when possible, and seek to bring them into the Light, for they follow a holy Mission, even if they know it not.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Cherion Group: </i>&quot;Excerpt from the Cherion Employee Handbook: Don't be a hero. Killing the specimen costs thousands of dollars, while a single live specimen can help save hundreds of lives. As well as earning a nice bonus.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:12:22-07:00","id":965172,"title":"","content":"<i>Canite Herasy: </i>Who are you talking about?<br /> <br /> <i>Les Mysteries: </i>While we stand at the crossroads they run from the path, blinded by glory. Remember your path, or you will share their fate. <br /> <br /> <i>Knights of Saint Adrian</i>: If you've got a problem with him I'll bring him in, that fool makes so much noise I won't even charge you, much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/963795-heroes-and-conspiracies?p=963979#post963979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Aegis Kai Doru</i>: &quot;They often claim to have magical talismans and relics that were recovered from the homes of these slain monsters, but all efforts to retrieve these relics for study have ended in failure. Further study is recommended.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I feel that given the age and experience of the AKD they should know by now exactly what the deal is with Heroes &quot;relics&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/963795-heroes-and-conspiracies?p=963979#post963979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[<i>Lucifuge</i>: &quot;Most of their targets seem to be living productive lives in the same way we do, using dark powers to protect people. I even met one that called me sister. He was cut down simply for being born different. Watch your back, unless these heroes decide we're part of it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Remember that while the Lucifgue are the most empathetic Conspiracy towards their prey, they still full time hunters and killers of monsters. They understand how being a monster can drive you towards evil, because they're monsters with a drive towards evil, but they don't accept evil behaviour from themselves or others. If they see a Beast hurting innocent people to feed, they'll understand why the beast does it, sympathise with the Beast, and hunt them down.<br /> <br /> (Within the usual bounds of moral complexity and hypocracy that all people and monsters have)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:55:01-07:00","id":965203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/963795-heroes-and-conspiracies?p=965172#post965172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that given the age and experience of the AKD they should know by now exactly what the deal is with Heroes &quot;relics&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they are a mystery cult. That's fine for reproducing the organisation, but I think it could reasonably limit their ability to gather information over the ages. I could see the AKD simply loosing a huge amount of information by mere turnover of members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T14:20:04-07:00","id":965263,"title":"","content":"I think you should draw a line between the theological elements of the AKD and practical information.<br /> <br /> Their secret history and things like that should be buried under layers of secrecy and only given to members who are &quot;worthy&quot;. But practical information like which Relic sword works best against a Vampire, or which monsters produce usable Relics and which ones produce things that only look like a Relic should be commonly available to the front line Hunters.<br /> <br /> Knowing that Hero's don't produce Relics is fairly basic information and, well, Conspiracy Tier hunters should have more information than and play fundamentally differently than Cell Tier Hunters. I mean, if they play the same what's the point of having two different types of Hunter? Even more importantly my personal interpretation of the AKD is strongly flavoured by Indiana Jones and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Librarian_(franchise)\" target=\"_blank\">The Liberian</a>: Ancient conspiracies, occult relics, archaeologists. It's all there - and it's even the first sample Hunter in the core book.<br /> <br /> So to me one of the core reasons the AKD exists is so your PCs can be trained in enough occult archaeology to solve the clues left behind by whatever ancient order has hidden this story's McGuffin. But if the AKD can provide it's members with enough knowledge to solve clues left behind by an long dead order then surely they can also give you basic information like Hero's &quot;Relics&quot; are just ordinary weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T02:15:07-07:00","id":965563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you should draw a line between the theological elements of the AKD and practical information. </div> </div> </div>It's the way the conspiracy is set up that's the problem. It's not exactly designed for easy dissemination of information. At best you're probably just going to be put in touch with someone else who has some experience of the problem. That's not a great way to pass coherent knowledge along.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/963795-heroes-and-conspiracies?p=965263#post965263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if the AKD can provide it's members with enough knowledge to solve clues left behind by an long dead order then surely they can also give you basic information like Hero's &quot;Relics&quot; are just ordinary weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that follows at all. Actually I'd be kinda sceptical of the AKD having a coherent view of Beasts in the first place. I mean, unless you have a special relic to investigate the Astral, all you have is what the Beasts say about themselves and that's not terribly coherent. Plus, there are probably plenty of things that look quite like Beasts but actually do involve relics; and generally the AKD aren't going to be able to tell the difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T04:00:51-07:00","id":965587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/963795-heroes-and-conspiracies?p=965172#post965172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff</div> </div> </div> </div> Ya know... why not make your own steroetypes up instead of trying to tell others how to interpret or play the game? If you don't like it, then please just make up a different quote and not threadcrap?<br /> <br /> The little stereotypes and blurbs are unrealistic in the first place. They're just fun little bits that are fun to read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-08-2016, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T04:44:49-07:00","id":965598,"title":"","content":"VASCU: &quot;Fundamentally, they are the vigilantes to our law enforcement, and frequently care little for whether their targets are truly criminal, nor for collateral damage. Most of them should be apprehended like any other preternatural killer.&quot;<br /> <br /> Habibi Ma: &quot;I take no issue with their quest or purpose, but some of them attract followers to themselves, and put those followers in harm's way. That sits ill with me.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Long Night: &quot;I understand what it is to have a purpose that cannot be set aside.&quot; [Version 2 adds: &quot;But that purpose should be dedicated to a greater end than one's own glory.&quot;]<br /> <br /> The Bear Lodge: &quot;If you can handle being the sidekick, these guys will lead you to a lot of challenging hunts.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Talbot Group: &quot;They slaughter possession victims who should be helped. Never trust them, never help them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maiden's Blood Sisterhood: &quot;The creatures they hunt thrive on violation, and have to be stopped For that alone, you sometimes have to work with them. But Christ, what a bunch of assholes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Night Watch: &quot;They show up, help kill dangerous shit, and move on to the next dangerous shit. My kind of guys.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Lucifuge: &quot;They have an evil nature, like us, but too often they let it rule them. But that goes for the Beasts they hunt as well. When you see a Hero, you're going to have to pick a side, and you won't know which until the times comes.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T06:01:08-07:00","id":965621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/963795-heroes-and-conspiracies?p=965563#post965563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the way the conspiracy is set up that's the problem. It's not exactly designed for easy dissemination of information. At best you're probably just going to be put in touch with someone else who has some experience of the problem. That's not a great way to pass coherent knowledge along.</div> </div> </div> </div> I can't remember anything that actually says how they're organised (the lack of a clear organisation section in the Compact/Conspiracy template is a major flaw I hope 2E corrects). But my thought was that between the Scroll being a research wing and the Temple dedicating itself to guarding storehouses; the AKD would be producing a fair amount of reserach and would have safe places to store that research.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/963795-heroes-and-conspiracies?p=965563#post965563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that follows at all.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why not? <br /> <br /> Being able to train an Indina Jones requires away of aquiring and preserving large amounts of information and a way of transmitting that information to new hunters.<br /> <br /> Once a Conspiracy has both of those features, it seems likely that it will acquire, preserve and transmit all sorts of useful information unrelated to archeology: Fire kills vampires, silver kills werewolves, Heroes don't create real Relics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/963795-heroes-and-conspiracies?p=965563#post965563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually I'd be kinda sceptical of the AKD having a coherent view of Beasts in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div> We know that there's a Beast focused hunter suppliment on the way. While we haven't seen anything from the AKD yet; every single *-focused Hunter suppliment has given the core 6 Conspiraces a coherent view on that book's prey.<br /> <br /> In fact you could make a good argument that the Hunter suppliments underplay how easy it is to mix up different kinds of monsters. I personally place it somewhere in the middle. Hunter organisations do know enough to have a different opinion on different types of monsters; however they still have to work hard (or have the right Endowment) to avoid ending up in a situation where they're trying to shoot a Gangrael who likes using Protean to turn into wolves with a silver bullet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/963795-heroes-and-conspiracies?p=965563#post965563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, unless you have a special relic to investigate the Astral</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a pretty safe bet that the AKD have lots of relics to investigate the Astral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T06:41:51-07:00","id":965638,"title":"","content":"Barrett Commission: &quot;They're uncomfortably noisy as allies, but effective in their own way, and seldom interested in any goals that would compete with our own.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey: &quot;It's a bit of a gamble, really. Their final battles end up really dull or really spectacular, without much in-between.&quot; [Obviously depending on whether the Hero chases the Beast into their Lair]<br /> <br /> Loyalists of Thule: &quot;They remind me of... well, you know.&quot;<br /> <br /> Keepers of the Source: &quot;I've heard of this cult of witches who go around killing the guardians of sacred sites.&quot; [A severe misunderstanding of how Beasts and Lairs relate, and I wanted to have one group making a charge against Heroes that's completely wrongheaded]<br /> <br /> Promethean Brotherhood: &quot;Best to let them get on with it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Utopia Now: &quot;Heroes, Beasts, bah. Chaos is chaos is chaos, I say. A plague on both their houses, if they could even think through building houses at all.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T03:30:02-07:00","id":967845,"title":"","content":"Network Zero; &quot;Most hunters play the monsters' games of secrecy. These guys want their vigil known; it's refreshing to see some of the others get it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Illuminated Brotherhood: &quot;Follow them, and you'll get the best vision quest of your life.&quot;<br /> <br /> Division Six: &quot;Effective. I wish we could turn them into our own targets.&quot;<br /> <br /> [I thought there should be a few more with a positive view of Heroes]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:02:41-07:00","id":968980,"title":"","content":"I could see various Compacts or Conspiracies approaching Heroes (and probably Beasts too) from a &quot;memetic threat&quot; perspective. The whole &quot;whipping up angry mobs&quot; thing might make a researcher extrapolate that &quot;heroism&quot; is somehow a contagious cognitohazard (I'm sorry for barfing all of this SCP-speak), leading them to treat Heroes as &quot;carriers&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}